        "original_id": "5b1eafc7-89bc-512f-9d00-42937e68f008",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Norman Z. McLeod, Sam Wanamaker, Wallace Beery, Marjorie Main\n- Works: Jackass Mail\n- Roles: film director, cartoonist, writer, actor\n- Places: Hollywood, the UK\n\nFacts:\n- Norman Zenos McLeod was born on September 20, 1898, and he was an American film director, cartoonist, and writer.\n- Samuel Wanamaker was born as Samuel Wattenmacker on June 14, 1919, and he was an American actor and director.\n- In 1942, Jackass Mail was released as a Western comedy film directed by Norman Z. McLeod and starring Wallace Beery and Marjorie Main.\n- Sam Wanamaker moved to the UK because he feared being blacklisted in Hollywood due to his early pronounced liberal sympathies.\n- Norman Z. McLeod died on January 27, 1964.\n- Sam Wanamaker died on December 18, 1993.",
